(Matrix Addition) Let A and B be two m x n matrices. 
Then their matrix sum A + B is the m x n matrix obtained by adding corresponding entries. 
THat is, the entry in the ith row jth column of A + B is a(sub(ij)) + b(sub(ij)), where a(sub(ij)) and b(sub(ij)) are the ijth entries of A and B, respectively
